      "key": "quickFacts",
      "source": "glaser",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.aquariumglaser.de/en/09-characoids-tetra-relationship/phenacogrammus_aurantiacus_en/",
      "html": "<p>A Congo tetra only 6-7 cm long, imported from the surroundings of Brazzaville. It is available in very small numbers only.</p>"
    },
    {
      "key": "distribution",
      "source": "glaser",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.aquariumglaser.de/en/09-characoids-tetra-relationship/phenacogrammus_aurantiacus_en/",
      "html": "<p>Imported from the surroundings of Brazzaville, Congo.</p>"
    },
    {
      "key": "notes",
      "source": "glaser",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.aquariumglaser.de/en/09-characoids-tetra-relationship/phenacogrammus_aurantiacus_en/",
      "html": "<p>This Congo tetra shows many somewhat unbelievable colours, depending on the light and the position of the fish. The basic colour is as follows: a brownish back with bright blue shining spots, followed by a bright shining horizontal band that can be orange, yellow or even greenish. Below that band is another broad horizontal band of leaden blue that also has many different reflecting colours. Then follows another orange-yellow-greenish zone, and finally the edge of the belly has bright blue spots.</p><p>The fins of the imported fish were still slightly damaged from transportation, but this will heal in a few days.</p>"
    }
  ],
